msgstr "一個字串或 ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1211
msgid ""
"Set the turtle shape to the named shape. If *name* is not given, return the "
"name of the current shape. The shape must exist in "
"the :class:`TurtleScreen`'s shape dictionary. Initially there are the "
"following shapes: \"arrow\", \"turtle\", \"circle\", \"square\", "
"\"triangle\" and \"classic\". To add shapes, see the :class:`Screen` "
"method :func:`register_shape`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1217
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'classic'\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"turtle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'turtle'"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'classic'\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"turtle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'turtle'"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1231
msgid ""
"Set the resizemode to \"auto\", \"user\" or \"noresize\". If *rmode* is not "
"given, return the current resizemode. The different resizemodes have the "
"following effects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1235
msgid ""
"\"auto\": the turtle is resized according to the value of :func:`pensize`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1236
msgid ""
"\"user\": the turtle is resized according to the stretch factors and outline "
"width, which are set by :func:`shapesize`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1238
msgid "\"noresize\": the turtle is not resized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1240
msgid ""
"``resizemode(\"user\")`` is called by :func:`shapesize` when used with "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1243
msgid ""
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'noresize'\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"auto\")\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'auto'"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'noresize'\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"auto\")\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'auto'"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1260
msgid ""
"Return or set the turtle's stretch factors and outline width. If no "
"arguments are given, return the current values. Otherwise set resizemode to "
"\"user\", so that the turtle is displayed stretched according to its stretch "
"factors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1265
msgid "*stretch_wid*: the stretch factor perpendicular to the turtle's heading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1266
msgid ""
"*stretch_len*: the stretch factor in the direction of the turtle's heading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1268
msgid "*outline*: the width of the shape's outline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1270
msgid ""
"For example, ``shapesize(2, 1)`` makes the turtle twice as wide without "
"changing its length. If only *stretch_wid* is given, *stretch_len* is set to "
"the same value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1274
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(1.0, 1.0, 1)\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"user\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(outline=8)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 8)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(1.0, 1.0, 1)\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"user\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(outline=8)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 8)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1292
msgid ""
"Return or set the current shear factor. Shearing slants the turtle shape, "
"like the slant of italic letters. The shear factor says how much it is "
"slanted: 0 is not slanted at all, and the larger the number, the stronger "
"the slant. Negative numbers slant the other way. If *shear* is not given, "
"return the current shear factor. Otherwise slant the turtle shape "
"accordingly and set resizemode to \"user\". The turtle's heading does not "
"change. Precisely, the shear factor is the tangent of the shear angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1300
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor()\n"
"0.5"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor()\n"
"0.5"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1314
msgid ""
"Turn the turtle shape by *angle* from its current tilt angle. The turtle's "
"heading does not change, so the turtle keeps moving in the same direction. "
"See :func:`tiltangle`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1318
msgid ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1334
msgid ""
"Return or set the current tilt angle. The tilt angle is the angle between "
"the direction the turtle shape points in and the direction the turtle moves "
"in. Normally the shape points in the direction of movement, so the tilt "
"angle is 0. If *angle* is given, turn the turtle shape to that tilt angle, "
"no matter what it was before, and set resizemode to \"user\". The turtle's "
"heading does not change. If *angle* is not given, return the current tilt "
"angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1342
msgid ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(45)\n"
">>> turtle.tiltangle()\n"
"45.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(45)\n"
">>> turtle.tiltangle()\n"
"45.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1360
msgid ""
"Return or set the transformation matrix of the turtle shape. The matrix "
"combines the stretch factors, the shear factor and the tilt angle of the "
"turtle shape into four numbers: *t11* and *t12* form its first row, *t21* "
"and *t22* its second. If none of them are given, return the current matrix "
"as a tuple of four numbers. Otherwise set the given elements and update the "
"stretch factors, shear factor and tilt angle accordingly. ``t11 * t22 - t12 "
"* t21`` must not be zero, otherwise an error is raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1368
msgid ""
">>> turtle = Turtle()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(4,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(-0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform()\n"
"(4.0, -1.0, -0.0, 2.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle = Turtle()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(4,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(-0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform()\n"
"(4.0, -1.0, -0.0, 2.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1381
msgid ""
"Return the points that form the outline of the current turtle shape as a "
"tuple of ``(x, y)`` coordinate pairs. These points can be used to define a "
"new shape or parts of a :ref:`compound shape <compound-shapes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1385
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform(4, -1, 0, 2)\n"
">>> turtle.get_shapepoly()\n"
"((50, -20), (30, 20), (-50, 20), (-30, -20))"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform(4, -1, 0, 2)\n"
">>> turtle.get_shapepoly()\n"
"((50, -20), (30, 20), (-50, 20), (-30, -20))"

